var n=Object.defineProperty;var o=(t,e)=>{for(var a in e)n(t,a,{get:e[a],enumerable:!0})};var d=[{text:"**Scenes and scripts** on a room's sheet: a button for each scene and script of the room's area (its own or its device's), and a tap runs it. A scene that locks, arms or opens a garage door asks first; scripts that need details are left out. Edit \u2192 **Selected** \u2192 **Scenes and scripts** hides some and adds others, also from another area or none.",anchor:"find-your-way-around"},{text:"**Search** (the magnifier over the buttons on the right, or **/** on a keyboard) finds a room, device, piece of furniture or scene by its name in Home Assistant, an alias, its area or its entity id. Picking one goes there, opens the room's sheet and points the device out with a pulsing marker.",anchor:"find-your-way-around"},{text:"**List of rooms and devices**: a new button on the right shows the house as a list of floors and rooms, with what their labels say, and the devices in them with their states. A room opens its sheet and a device switches as a tap on it does. It is how a keyboard or a screen reader gets around the house.",anchor:"find-your-way-around"},{text:"Keyboard and screen readers: a ring shows where the keyboard is, sheets, menus and the sun and weather panel take the focus when they open and **Escape** closes them, every button and field has a name, and what a tap did and new alerts are read out once.",anchor:"find-your-way-around"},{text:"**Gates that open**: a gate's **Opener** (a cover, lock, switch or contact sensor) opens and closes it in 3D, swinging to either side or sliding along the fence (**Swings**, **Slides**, **Flip hinge**, **Swing other way**). A tap on the gate asks first, with **Open**, **Close**, **Stop** and a position slider for a cover, as it can do them.",anchor:"fences-and-garden-walls"},{text:"**Awnings** (in **Garden**) run out and back with their cover, and a tap asks first like a gate's.",anchor:"by-hand"},{text:"A window's blind that reports a tilt is drawn as a **venetian blind** with its slats at that angle, and a **roof window** can have a **Blind**, and a motorised window's cover as its **Sensor**.",anchor:"by-hand"},{text:"Blinds, gates and awnings move smoothly (at a gate's pace while one only says it is opening or closing), draw nothing once they have stopped, and jump with reduce motion turned on.",anchor:null}];export{o as a,d as b};
